## Slide 1

Template Systems

## Slide 2

Template Systems 

Used to facilitate rapid modeling of Manufacturing Equipment that produce/process similar products and have similar data requirements
Can be created for each type of System (Batch, Discrete, and Storage)
Template Parents contain configuration elements identical to the non-template versions
Most properties are configured on the Template Parent and are locked on the Template Children
Template Parents are for configuration only and do not produce data

## Slide 3

Creating a Parent Template System

Template Parents can be created from scratch, or from an existing non-template System
When creating from scratch:
All properties will start with the defaults and must be configured individually
All Tags will need to be configured and assigned to the Parent manually
When creating from an existing non-template System:
A “Template Tag Prefix” should be configured on the non-template System
A “Parent Template Tag Prefix” must be provided
A target “Tag Group ID” must be provided
Matching Template Tags will be created automatically for the new Template Parent

## Slide 4

Configuring a Template System

Available properties will be the same as a normal system of the same type
Properties relating to the way data is process and recorded will be configured on the Template Parent
Types
Script Classes
Event Logic
Properties relating to defining or recording context will be configured individually the Template Children
Schedules
Product Sets
Production Scheduling Sets
Tags will be configured using Template Tag Mapping

Template Parent
Template Child

## Slide 5

Template Tag Mapping 

Template Parent Systems will use Template Tags for all tag-based properties
Template Children Systems can use any tag type for tag-based properties
Template Children cannot have tags directly assigned to them through their configuration. They must use one of the Assign Tags actions.
Template tag prefix is required for the mapping to take place
Tag Duplication can be utilized to quickly prepare tags for new template children, but will not be effective for all Tag Types

